  "summary": "Poro-society masks, rhythm pounders and kponyugu fire-spitter helmets of Senufo carver families.",
  "description": "Senufo carvers — the sculptor caste serving poro initiation society — produced one of West Africa's most recognizable repertoires: kponyugu fire-spitter helmet masks blending crocodile jaw, warthog tusks and antelope horns; serene kpelie face masks with swung side lobes; tall female rhythm pounders (deble) whose elongated bodies drummed mortuary mortars; and birds of prophecy — the \"bird of the poro\" with hooked beak and nest-belly. Blackened dense wood, few pigments, perfect proportion — Picasso-era collectors named Senufo sculpture \"classical\" African art.",
